hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1524","Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala’ and Sa’id bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Makhzoumi told us, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, he said: I heard a narration Mawla of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: “I spent the night at my aunt Maimuna’s, and he, meaning the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed as long as God wished, then He lay down and slept until he blew, then the muezzin came to him calling him to prayer, so he went out and prayed.” This is the hadith of Abdul-Jabbar"
